  "facts": [
    "Bømlafjord Tunnel, opened 27 December 2000, stretches 7.82 km beneath Bømlafjorden, reaching 260.4 m below sea level—making it Norway's deepest subsea road tunnel at the time of its completion.",
    "Construction teams blasted from opposite ends, breaking through 5 May 1999 and achieving breakthrough on 2 September 1999—five months ahead of schedule—while averaging 55 m per week and once reaching 96.7 m in a single week.",
    "Until 30 April 2013, the tunnel operated as a toll road, collecting fees that funded its 2000 opening, after which tolls were abolished, leaving the 4,084‑vehicle‑per‑day traffic to flow freely."
  ],
